# CodeAtlas MCP server (Codex CLI)

Codex CLI reads MCP servers from `~/.codex/config.toml`. Add:

```toml
[mcp_servers.codeatlas]
command = "codeatlas-chatgpt-mcp"
args = ["--root", "/absolute/path/to/your/project"]

[mcp_servers.codeatlas.env]
ATLAS_ROOT = "/absolute/path/to/your/project"
```

The server is the same binary used for the ChatGPT connector; only the
transport differs (`--http` for ChatGPT, default stdio for Codex).

To let CodeAtlas register this automatically, run `atlas agents connect`
(from `codeatlas-cli`), which writes the equivalent entry for every installed,
supported agent.
